{"alignments":[],"candidates":[{"additionalConceptCount":0,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, the longest side","reason":"If a²+b²=c² for positive side lengths, then c² exceeds both a² and b², so c must be the longest side.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_178_q2","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"cnm_178_q2_m1","label":"Identify the candidate hypotenuse","methodDirectNodeIds":{"cnm_178_q2_m1":["cnm_177"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_177"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: I, II, and III","reason":"The first three satisfy 3^2+4^2 = 5^2, 4^2+7.5^2 = 8.5^2, and 7^2+24^2 = 25^2. For IV, 3.5^2+4.5^2 = 32.5, not 5.5^2 = 30.25.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1972_AMC_12_Q01","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_174"],"id":"test-squared-side-lengths","label":"Test the longest side","methodDirectNodeIds":{"test-squared-side-lengths":["cnm_177"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_177","cnm_174"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, yes","reason":"5²+12²=25+144=169=13², so the converse of the Pythagorean theorem establishes a right triangle.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_177_q1","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_021"],"id":"cnm_177_q1_m1","label":"Check the longest side","methodDirectNodeIds":{"cnm_177_q1_m1":["cnm_177"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_177","cnm_021"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A: (6, 8, 10)","reason":"6²+8²=36+64=100=10². Although 0.3²+0.4²=0.5², those numbers are not positive integers and therefore are not a Pythagorean triple.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_177_q2","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_003","cnm_021"],"id":"cnm_177_q2_m1","label":"Apply the definition of a Pythagorean triple","methodDirectNodeIds":{"cnm_177_q2_m1":["cnm_177"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_177","cnm_003","cnm_021"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, right triangle","reason":"Expanding and canceling 2ab gives a²+b²=c². Thus c is the longest side and the triangle is right.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_177_q4","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_040"],"id":"cnm_177_q4_m1","label":"Reveal the Pythagorean relation","methodDirectNodeIds":{"cnm_177_q4_m1":["cnm_148","cnm_177"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_148","cnm_177","cnm_040"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":2,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, yes; hypotenuse √5","reason":"(√2)²+(√3)²=2+3=5=(√5)², so the triangle is right with hypotenuse √5.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_178_q1","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_168","cnm_079"],"id":"cnm_178_q1_m1","label":"Square the radical side lengths","methodDirectNodeIds":{"cnm_178_q1_m1":["cnm_177"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_177","cnm_168","cnm_079"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 13.5","reason":"Because 1.5²+2²=2.5², triangle EPD is right and has area 1.5. Also PA=4 and PC=3. The areas of AEP, EPD, DPC, and CPA are respectively 2, 1, 2, and 4 times the area of EPD, so AEDC has area 9·1.5=13.5.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2013_AMC_10B_Q16","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_113","cnm_p148","cnm_p150"],"id":"perpendicular-medians","label":"Perpendicular medians and triangle areas","methodDirectNodeIds":{"perpendicular-media